---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const description = "Run the L1 policy against your app and explore the separate scanner regression matrix.";
---
<Base title="Benchmark | Insidia Labs" description={description} path="/benchmark">
  <Header />
  <main id="content" class="wrap" style="padding:3rem 0 4rem">
    <p class="kicker">Policy</p>
    <h1>The Insidia Benchmark</h1>
    <p class="lede">Run a policy against your app, or explore the public matrix used to test scanner adapters. They provide different kinds of evidence.</p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Policy</h2>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>L1 baseline</h3>
        <p>Checks that need no model. This is what <code>insidia init</code> writes and what a scan runs. Use it on every pull request. The process exits 1 when the policy fails. L2 and L3 are not available.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What a run writes</h2>
      <p><code>insidia scan --policy L1</code> writes a directory under <code>.insidia/runs/</code>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>benchmark.json</code> — policy name, pass or fail, control results, and skips</li>
        <li><code>findings.json</code> — each finding names its engine, probe, severity, and taxonomy</li>
        <li><code>results.sarif</code> — for code scanning in CI</li>
        <li><code>report.html</code> — one file, opened with <code>insidia report --open</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Controls map to OWASP LLM, OWASP Agentic, and OWASP Web and API where the registry has a mapping. MITRE ATLAS is not mapped yet. A framework score is the controls that ran, not a percentage we market on this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The scanner matrix</h2>
      <p>The repository holds sandboxed targets with planted vulnerabilities and a permutation matrix for testing adapters and transports. Passing these fixtures is a regression check; it does not establish detector accuracy on real applications or release readiness. Independent validation is part of the current productization work.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/Rushi-Balapure/Insidia-Labs/tree/main/benchmark">Read the benchmark directory</a> · <a href="/#install">Install the CLI</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
